{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments","id":977093,"title":"Which spells are best as Legacy Attainments?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-27T03:41:33-07:00","id":977093,"title":"Which spells are best as Legacy Attainments?","content":"I am designing legacies for my characters and quite often have to stop and think about whether a certain spell should be an attainment, or if that spell is better left as a spell.<br /> <br /> So what are your thoughts about what spells are best as Attainments? Because of the way Attainments work rules-wise - no dispellation and no spell slot required - I see spells that boost and buff the mage, especially long-term, as the better ones. Summoning spells MIGHT count as such as well, but probably not all the time since Attainments have lackluster Reach. So, mainly spells that use the Shielding, Weaving and Patterning Practice. Spells that use the Practices of Unveiling, Knowing, Compelling and Ruling seem better left as spells as they really do not benefit from the advantages that Attainments have over spells.<br /> <br /> But that may be just me, right? Do any of you have contrasting experiences of the possibilities and limitations of Legacy Attainments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T03:48:45-07:00","id":977097,"title":"","content":"Direct damage spells are also pretty potent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T03:57:02-07:00","id":977098,"title":"","content":"Direct damage spells seem to me like rather lacklustre as Attainments as well, seeing as if they are cast as spells you can calibrate the damage and easily add more reach to cause Tilts. The main difference is that Attainment damage does not suffer Paradox, but a mage that runs around casting such things among sleepers is not safe in my campaigns unless special effort is made to have it look mundane or hide it... which you can already do with spells anyway.<br /> <br /> I know that RAW Attainments do not cause Wisdom rolls, which is a rule I sometimes ignore because it doesn't really make sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:00:36-07:00","id":977099,"title":"","content":"Sorry, didn't know we were talking about your homebrew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:05:27-07:00","id":977100,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd say figure out the &quot;story&quot; or concept of your legacy, then pick spells core to that. Unless optimizing is part of the concept, it seems backwards to pick just spells that game the system best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:06:53-07:00","id":977101,"title":"","content":"I am not talking about a homebrew. Please consider my remark about Wisdom degeneration as a parenthesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:09:41-07:00","id":977103,"title":"","content":"Combined spell attainments are also pretty good since you can sometimes work them to avoid some of the Reach problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:14:09-07:00","id":977104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977100#post977100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd say figure out the &quot;story&quot; or concept of your legacy, then pick spells core to that. Unless optimizing is part of the concept, it seems backwards to pick just spells that game the system best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it may seem backwards to do so and I agree. Most of the time I look to flavor and theme when designing Attainments, though I also tend to go with the reasoning that it is the fittest legacies - those that best utilize their resources and strengths - that survive the test of time and attract new members.<br /> <br /> Most of all I am curious to know if there are aspects and important details I have missed that hamper my experience with Legacies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:25:55-07:00","id":977112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977103#post977103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combined spell attainments are also pretty good since you can sometimes work them to avoid some of the Reach problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I do not recognize this concept! Where can I read up on combining attainments? In Mage I can only find things about combining spells and praxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:29:27-07:00","id":977113,"title":"","content":"Long-term buffs work well as attainments, freeing up spell control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:42:39-07:00","id":977118,"title":"","content":"I have to agree that direct damage spells seem fairly anemic as Attainments. Guaranteed success with X potency is certainly nice, but the very earliest you can get it is as a third Attainment, requiring Gnosis 4 and Arcanum 3, for &lt;Arcanum&gt; automatic bashing damage; if you were instead casting it as a spell, you'd be looking at a base dice pool of 7; a Potency 3 Fraying spell would have you rolling 3 dice even before adding Yantras and such. And, well, Bashing damage is not exactly going to bring the house down. A four-dot Attainment can get you Lethal damage, but at that point you're Gnosis 6 and you can <i>definitely</i> get something better with your regular spellcasting. And the errata looks set to make a hypothetical direct damage Attainment even weaker, taking the primary spell factor from &lt;primary arcanum&gt; to &lt;primary arcanum minus one&gt;. The one potential advantage I see of direct-damage Legacy Attainments is the ability to tack on extra Scale as a secondary spell factor, but it doesn't seem very strong to me.<br /> <br /> Spells that allow the target to Withstand them (curses, mind-reading, mental influence, and such) are also problematic, on account of the fixed Potency (and will get even more so with the errata). Even against a resistance stat of 2, you need 3 dots in the relevant Arcanum to do anything at all, and anything that increases the relevant stat will quickly push you out of range.<br /> <br /> So what you want, for a potent Attainment, is a spell that a) you'll want to have active often, to take advantage of the free Spell Control, b) that isn't Withstood, c) that doesn't need a lot of Reach to be good. Which seems to me to mostly mean, as you say, self-buffs of one sort or another; long-term ones let you have them up constantly without spell control difficulties, and short-term ones of the form &quot;get +Potency to &lt;roll&gt;&quot; can be nice to have guaranteed success of decent Potency on.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is warding effects, like Ward, Ban, Shield of Chronos, and the like. The fixed Potency is of little concern, because they <i>cannot be dispelled</i>. They just stick around until the duration expires. And you can just throw them around like confetti, because spell control? What spell control? You do need to allocate Reach to Advanced Duration if you want them to be around long enough to be relevant, but hey, can't have everything. Besides, even if you only have one Reach available for the Attainment and therefore have to make it a ritual, an hour or so to set up an un-dispellable ward that doesn't count against spell control seems like a pretty good deal to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977100#post977100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd say figure out the &quot;story&quot; or concept of your legacy, then pick spells core to that. Unless optimizing is part of the concept, it seems backwards to pick just spells that game the system best.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO, at least, some level of optimisation ought to be part of the concept for anything being developed by mages. Especially something as serious as a Legacy. You're talking about shaping your very being; is any mage going to do that for something that they could do better with normal magic? It seems implausible to me. A Legacy Attainment that doesn't offer <i>some</i> kind of reasonable advantage over casting a spell is unlikely to ever be developed, and if developed, is unlikely to find anyone interested in learning it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:51:52-07:00","id":977123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977112#post977112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I do not recognize this concept! Where can I read up on combining attainments? In Mage I can only find things about combining spells and praxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds to me like he's suggesting an Attainment that duplicates a combined spell effect? I too am intrigued by the possibilities and interested in hearing more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T05:18:47-07:00","id":977126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977112#post977112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I do not recognize this concept! Where can I read up on combining attainments? In Mage I can only find things about combining spells and praxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's implied in the last attainment of the 11Q, the Optional Matter attainment spends too much Reach being Instant and at Sensory range of it's a stand alone effect. Combined with the scene long activation of the Time attainment it falls back into complained with the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:02:23-07:00","id":977284,"title":"","content":"Good:<br /> - Any long duration buffing spells (saves you spell control)<br /> - Any spell that generally risks wisdom -&gt; Mind Control spell, soul stealing, damage spells<br /> - Any spell you <i>really</i> don't want counterspelled or dispelled -&gt; anything that keeps you alive or can be used as an emergency escape spell<br /> <br /> Great example of something that fits all three is an advanced duration damage spell. Without having to spend spell control or risking Widsom you deal your arcanum in damage every hour for up to a week, with no way of dispelling it or getting rid of it.<br /> <br /> Bad:<br /> - Any instant cast spell cast spell that doesn't risk wisdom and that enemies have no reason to try and counterspell -&gt; Know Spirit and similar spells<br /> - Any spell that needs both a good duration and a good potency, or lots of Reach.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:36:59-07:00","id":977750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977284#post977284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great example of something that fits all three is an advanced duration damage spell. Without having to spend spell control or risking Widsom you deal your arcanum in damage every hour for up to a week, with no way of dispelling it or getting rid of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only really worth it as a 4th or 5th Attainment, since Bashing Damage would generally heal by time it is inflicted again. Unless it is <i>meant</i> to just make someone miserable and degrade normal healing (since they couldn't heal any <i>new</i> Bashing Damage while they are still dealing with the Attainment inflicted ones).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:41:54-07:00","id":977755,"title":"","content":"Time between damage tick overs would decrease as your Gnosis increased though. So eventually if you raised it enough even Bashing damage would kill most targets pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:33:26-07:00","id":977782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977755#post977755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time between damage tick overs would decrease as your Gnosis increased though. So eventually if you raised it enough even Bashing damage would kill most targets pretty quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Right. So, since the 3rd Attainment is minimum Gnosis 4 (1 Hour). Potency would be 3, for 3 Bashing (every hour). Bashing heals every 15 minutes, so they'd be completely healed by the time of the next interval (though if they took additional Bashing, they'd effectively only heal that at a rate of 1 per hour, due to the 3 from the Attainment). Reach would only be limited to 1 as a 3rd Attainment, so I'm assuming it would be to push the duration to Advanced. The Attainment would take a Scene to prep. Potency scales with Arcanum. Duration scales with Arcanum (1 day at Arcanum 3, 1 week at Arcanum 4+, due to Advanced Duration).<br /> <br /> Assuming no change in Arcanum rating..<br /> Gnosis 5: Every 30 minutes. At this point, the Bashing damage will ever-so-slowly kill someone throughout the day. Since they have a net of 1 Bashing ever 30 minutes, at about 2.5hrs (for the average Health of 7), the bashing will roll over into Lethal, and the downward death spiral begins. It should take another 2 hrs to fill them with Lethal and trigger Bleeding Out. However, this all assumes a base 15 minutes to heal Bashing. Medical care (or anything that boosts Healing times) will dramatically affect the math. One such boost allows the target to recover 4 Bashing every 30 minutes instead of 2, beating or tying the damage inflicted until Arcanum 5.<br /> Gnosis 7: Every 10 minutes. Death in short order. Since the average person can only regain 1 Bashing every two intervals, they'll be comatose and dying inside the hour. Quick Healing can reduce the effect, but not by much, unless stacked.<br /> Gnosis 9: Every minute. Yeah, pretty much dead before they can even start to heal the Bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:38:44-07:00","id":977807,"title":"","content":"I forget, does healing reset if you take damage for the wound in question (but not other wounds)? I thought that was a point of interest but I'm not able to look it up right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:39:23-07:00","id":977808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977750#post977750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's only really worth it as a 4th or 5th Attainment,<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>5th, really. Didn't say it was a low level one!<br /> <br /> Edit: I assumed that damage intervall for this spell is bound to the &quot;ritual cast&quot; time for Attainments, which is fixed at 1 scene/hour. If it scales with Gnosis that makes this attainment workable with bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 09-28-2016, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:50:59-07:00","id":977812,"title":"","content":"Legacies are about eternally altering your soul towards some direction you believe in, that serves your Obsessions. Forging your soul into a weapon of mass destruction is making a pretty loud statement.<br /> <br /> I see the mechanical advantage of it, but there's a lot you can do with legacies that can't be replicated by bringing a gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:04:24-07:00","id":977818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977812#post977812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacies are about eternally altering your soul towards some direction you believe in, that serves your Obsessions. Forging your soul into a weapon of mass destruction is making a pretty loud statement.<br /> <br /> I see the mechanical advantage of it, but there's a lot you can do with legacies that can't be replicated by bringing a gun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an example of a spell that makes use of several of the advantages a legacy attainment offers, not ' take this attainment' min-max guide!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:10:11-07:00","id":977820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977818#post977818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was an example of a spell that makes use of several of the advantages a legacy attainment offers, not ' take this attainment' min-max guide!</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to agree with your original statement, but all your example of a 'good' spell were situated towards combat, and the example obviously was.<br /> <br /> Another 'good' spell is something that creates. Objects and illusions and other obvious magical effects created via legacy attainment do not suffer dissonance. The bokor are a good example of this, creating zombies that would normally be run down by their Supernal power in the Fallen World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-28-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:22:46-07:00","id":977826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977820#post977820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was going to agree with your original statement, but all your example of a 'good' spell were situated towards combat, and the example obviously was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been spending some time translating the immortal weapons into legacies, colors my examples<br /> &gt;_&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 09-28-2016, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:32:13-07:00","id":977831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977826#post977826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been spending some time translating the immortal weapons into legacies, colors my examples<br /> &gt;_</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a problem, you aren't wrong, damaging spells as attainments have great advantages, especially with the freedom from Hubris and paradox. It's just there's more to it.<br /> <br /> Have you posted these translations? Or will you, when you're done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:39:34-07:00","id":977835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977807#post977807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget, does healing reset if you take damage for the wound in question (but not other wounds)? I thought that was a point of interest but I'm not able to look it up right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you cast a healing spell with advanced duration it just continues to activate to heal damage once per GRI even if there isn't any there to heal in which case it effectively does nothing. It doesn't differentiate between wounds except as categories B, L, or A. Although a spell set to heal A would heal B and L by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-28-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:40:45-07:00","id":977836,"title":"","content":"Definitely, it's just really slow going thanks to Real Life and games interfering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:05:28-07:00","id":977847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977835#post977835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you cast a healing spell with advanced duration it just continues to activate to heal damage once per GRI even if there isn't any there to heal in which case it effectively does nothing. It doesn't differentiate between wounds except as categories B, L, or A. Although a spell set to heal A would heal B and L by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> meant normal healing.<br /> <br /> But there's a great idea for an Attainment - Healing. Since Attainments are immune to Paradox, you can heal Sleepers without worry, and even fully regenerate limbs without fear of dispelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:55:48-07:00","id":977872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977847#post977847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> meant normal healing.<br /> <br /> But there's a great idea for an Attainment - Healing. Since Attainments are immune to Paradox, you can heal Sleepers without worry, and even fully regenerate limbs without fear of dispelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that. I guess the Rules-as-Written (sorry I hate acronyms) say that healing and taking damage calculates together, but I could have sworn I read somewhere about it not doing that, which would kind of make sense. I mean, lets say you got stabbed for 2Lethal and a day later someone stabbed you in the same place, it could undo the healing you've been doing and you'd have to restart healing that wound.<br /> <br /> I should probably spend less time thinking of fringe scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:03:56-07:00","id":977875,"title":"","content":"That would just be represented by additional L done by the stabbing even if it was in the exact same spot. Most of the time I'm pretty sure the rules don't call for something so specific to represent where you've been hit, when they do they're Tilts or Conditions generally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:04:16-07:00","id":977876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/977093-which-spells-are-best-as-legacy-attainments?p=977872#post977872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that. I guess the Rules-as-Written (sorry I hate acronyms) say that healing and taking damage calculates together, but I could have sworn I read somewhere about it not doing that, which would kind of make sense. I mean, lets say you got stabbed for 2Lethal and a day later someone stabbed you in the same place, it could undo the healing you've been doing and you'd have to restart healing that wound.<br /> <br /> I should probably spend less time thinking of fringe scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering that you heal from the &quot;right&quot; and gain damage from the &quot;left&quot;, getting new damage fills a &quot;new&quot; box on the right, which would then start healing (taking the required time depending on its severity).<br /> <br /> For my calculations above, with Bashing, the Damage from the Attainment comes in blocks all at once, then the target starts healing the &quot;right-most&quot;. At Arcanum 3, Gnosis 4, they heal all of the damage from one interval, before the next group arrives. At Gnosis 5+, they heal 2 Bashing, then another 3+ get added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}